      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The use of 6 French guiding catheters is still usually limited to elective percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. We describe our preliminary experience with this guiding size to perform a double guide wire procedure for angioplasty or coronary bifurcation lesions, to protect (n = 5) and/or to sequentially dilate (n = 9) a major side branch. Technical success was 12/14 (86%), angiographic success 13/14 (93%), and in-hospital outcome was event free in all patients. Thus, 6 French guiding size is both safe and effective for the majority of coronary bifurcation angioplasty."},
